By: enliteme

Hi there,

Do you have some specific reason to compile rkward from source?
Because you can install it through YaST.

I had some problems with rkward using KDE 4 (icons disappeared) both in Suse
and in Ubuntu.
I think OpenSUSE 11 comes with KDE 4 by default. (but you can switch back to
KDE3 or to Gnome).
I had no problem installing/using rkward with KDE 3 though...
So, it can be a problem with KDE4... 

By the way, reading your error message, I would start by checking if I have
the correct compiler installed.

> which c++
or
> which gcc

or whatever it is specified in the docs.

Good luck,

gabor



